>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does gas hob installation cost in Liverpool?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">£120 including VAT to fit a gas hob you supply, where a gas point is already in place. A freestanding gas cooker connected is also £120.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Gas hob fitted</strong></td><td>£120</td><td>You supply the hob. Gas point in place.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Gas cooker connected</strong></td><td>£120</td><td>Freestanding cooker on a bayonet hose.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Disconnect and cap</strong></td><td>£120 first hour</td><td>Weekdays 9am–4pm. £150 evenings and weekends.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>New or moved gas point</strong></td><td>Free visit</td><td>Fixed written price before we start.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>There is no call-out fee. If we find something that needs extra work, such as a worn gas pipe, we tell you the price before we carry on. You can say no.</p>
      <p>Got other jobs too? Our first hour often covers a few small jobs. See our <a href="/small-plumbing-jobs-liverpool">small plumbing jobs</a> page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="law">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do I need a Gas Safe engineer to fit a gas hob?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Under the Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations, only a Gas Safe registered engineer may fit or connect a gas appliance for you.</p>
      <p>That includes gas hobs and gas cookers. It also includes taking one out and capping the pipe. A poor joint can leak gas. A badly set hob can make carbon monoxide.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Ask to see the engineer's Gas Safe ID card. It shows what they can work on.</li>
        <li>Check the card says they are qualified for cookers and hobs.</li>
        <li>You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register before they start.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Most hob makers also say the hob must be fitted by a Gas Safe engineer. If it is not, the warranty may not count.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Kitchen fitters:</strong> many are not Gas Safe registered. That is fine. Your fitter can cut the worktop, and our Gas Safe registered engineers make the gas connection.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included when you fit a gas hob?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">The full job: we connect the hob, test the gas for leaks and check every burner works safely. Then we show you how to use it.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>The fitting</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Old hob disconnected and taken out</li>
            <li>New hob seated and sealed in the worktop</li>
            <li>Connected to your gas point the way the maker says</li>
            <li>A gas isolation valve, so it can be turned off on its own</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>The safety checks</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>A gas tightness test on the whole supply</li>
            <li>Gas pressure checked at the hob</li>
            <li>Every burner lit, with a clean, steady flame</li>
            <li>Flame safety cut-outs tested where fitted</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">We also check the space around the hob is right for the model, such as the gap to the cooker hood. A record of the work is emailed the same day.</p>
      <figure class="sg-photo" style="max-width:360px;margin-top:1.25rem;">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/gas-hob-oven-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/gas-hob-oven-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 360px" />
          <img src="/images/jobs/gas-hob-oven-fitted-960.jpg" alt="Gas hob and oven fitted in a Liverpool kitchen" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </picture>
        <figcaption>A gas hob and oven fitted by our team in a Liverpool kitchen.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does gas hob fitting work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Book, we arrive, we fit and test. A like-for-like swap takes about an hour.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Call or book online.</strong> Tell us the hob model and where the gas point is. A photo helps. We confirm the price. (5 minutes)</li>
        <li><strong>We arrive.</strong> We turn the gas off and check the old hob and pipe. If the price would change, we tell you first.</li>
        <li><strong>We fit the new hob.</strong> It is seated in the worktop and connected to the gas. (About 30 minutes)</li>
        <li><strong>We test it.</strong> A gas tightness test, then every burner is lit and checked. (About 15 minutes)</li>
        <li><strong>All done.</strong> We show you how it works, take the old hob away if you want and email you a record.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>New hob arriving this week?</strong> Call and we will book it in.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If your old gas hob or cooker sits in the same place as the new one, it is the £120 fixed price. If the gas has to go somewhere new, book a free visit.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Your kitchen</th><th>What you need</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Swapping an old gas hob for a new one</td><td>Gas hob fitted</td><td>£120</td></tr>
            <tr><td>New freestanding gas cooker</td><td>Gas cooker connected</td><td>£120</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Moving house or going electric</td><td>Disconnect and cap</td><td>£120 first hour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>New kitchen with the hob in a new spot</td><td>New or moved gas point</td><td>Free visit, then fixed price</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Electric cooker now, want gas</td><td>New gas point</td><td>Free visit, then fixed price</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Not sure? Send us a photo of the gas point behind your old hob or cooker. We will tell you which one it is.</p>
      <p>Going from gas to induction? We cap the gas. The new hob usually needs its own electric circuit. Our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk/">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> can fit that.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="cooker">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Gas cooker installation and disconnection</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We connect freestanding gas cookers for £120, and we disconnect and cap gas cookers and hobs when you move or change.</p>
      <h3>Gas cooker connection</h3>
      <p>A freestanding gas cooker connects with a bayonet hose. It plugs into a socket on the wall, so the cooker can be pulled out to clean. We fit a new hose if yours is old, worn or the wrong length.</p>
      <p>We also fit a stability chain or bracket. This stops the cooker tipping forward if someone leans on the open oven door. Then we test for leaks and check the hob, oven and grill.</p>
      <h3>Gas hobs are different</h3>
      <p>A built-in gas hob is usually hard-piped in copper. Some makers allow a special approved flexible hose. We follow what the maker's instructions say for your model.</p>
      <h3>Disconnect a gas cooker or hob</h3>
      <p>Moving out, or taking the old cooker with you? We disconnect it, cap the gas pipe and test it is sealed. This is covered by our first hour: £120 on weekdays 9am–4pm, £150 evenings and weekends.</p>
      <p>We do not fit, service or check gas fires. If you have an old one you no longer use, we can disconnect and cap it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="before">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What should I do before you arrive?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Check the hob runs on natural gas, keep the box and instructions, and clear the cupboard under the hob.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Natural gas or LPG?</strong> Most Liverpool homes are on natural gas (G20). Check the hob box says so.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep the instructions.</strong> We fit it the way the maker sets out.</li>
        <li><strong>Worktop cut-out.</strong> A new kitchen should have the hole cut to the hob's size. On a swap, we check the new hob fits the old hole.</li>
        <li><strong>Clear the space.</strong> Empty the cupboard below so we can reach the gas point.</li>
        <li><strong>Landlords.</strong> We can arrange access with your tenant and do the yearly <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-liverpool">gas safety certificate</a> on the same visit.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger">
        <p><strong>Smell gas?</strong> Do not use the hob or any light switches. Open windows, turn the gas off at the meter if it is safe, get everyone out and ring the National Gas Emergency line on <a href="tel:08001119999">0800 111 999</a>. Once it is made safe, our <a href="/emergency-gas-engineer-liverpool">emergency gas engineers</a> can find and fix the fault.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
